<article class="env-definition" id="024A">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/024A">Definition <span data-tag="024A">85.27.3</span>.</a> Let $f : X \to S$ be a morphism of schemes. The <em>simplicial scheme associated to $f$</em>, denoted $(X/S)_\bullet $, is the functor $\Delta ^{opp} \to \mathit{Sch}$, $[n] \mapsto X \times _ S \ldots \times _ S X$ described in Simplicial, Example <a href="/tag/016E" data-tag="016E">14.3.5</a>. </p>
</article>